description:
## Problem
Verification reach beyond DuckDB, ClickHouse and Snowflake is undecided. The corpus shows zero tuned runs on other platforms.

## Change
Implement exactly what gate D-9 decides. If facts-only is chosen, build a generic per-platform catalog-facts reader with no verdicts. Otherwise, build introspectors only for the platforms the gate admits, each only after that platform's render-at-execution item lands.

Per-platform structured sources:
- Databricks `DESCRIBE DETAIL` (`clusteringColumns`, `partitionColumns`);
- BigQuery `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS`;
- Redshift `SVV_TABLE_INFO` / `PG_TABLE_DEF`;
- PostgreSQL `pg_index` / `pg_partitioned_table`;
- StarRocks `information_schema.tables_config`;
- Trino / Iceberg `$properties` / `$partitions`;
- Firebolt `information_schema.indexes`;
- Synapse `sys.pdw_*`;
- MotherDuck `duckdb_indexes()`.

## Guardrails (must preserve)
- Bounded: the ledger-table filter goes inside the SQL `WHERE` and truncation is measured on the raw result. Fix the ClickHouse introspector, which computes `truncated` after filtering (`clickhouse/introspection.py:73,81`).
- Non-raising, structured catalogs only (never DDL text).
- Recorded-fixture unit tests, plus a separately approved live confirmation per platform.

## Process guardrails
- One PR per item against `develop`, via the AGENTS.md worktree flow (`make worktree-claim BRANCH=...`, `make agent-write-preflight`).
- Verification ladder: `uv run -- python -m pytest -m fast -q`, `uv run -- ruff check .`, `uv run -- ruff format --check .` and `uv run -- ty check`.
- Then `make pr-preflight` and `make pr-open`.
- Stage explicit paths; never `git add -A`.
- No live cloud runs without explicit user approval stating the command, maximum runtime, log path and stop condition.
- Re-read every file:line anchor before editing. Anchors are from develop d39166ea.
